"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:27:10-08:00","id":1040849,"title":"","content":"In what sense are you using 'Divine'? Are you referring to using Space to spy on them sympathetically? Time to gaze into their past or future? Fate to take a look at their destiny?<br /> <br /> I suppose the short answer is: very yes. Mages are investigators, and the first dot of every Arcana provides Knowning and Unveiling magics excellent for all kinds of divinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:31:08-08:00","id":1040852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040843-divination-and-awakening?p=1040849#post1040849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what sense are you using 'Divine'? Are you referring to using Space to spy on them sympathetically? Time to gaze into their past or future? Fate to take a look at their destiny?<br /> <br /> I suppose the short answer is: very yes. Mages are investigators, and the first dot of every Arcana provides Knowning and Unveiling magics excellent for all kinds of divinations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I am referring to the Time Spell Divination, which seems pretty powerful and open. I assumed the answer was yes, but it seemed kind of interesting since in 1E that was assumed impossible.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:36:16-08:00","id":1040857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040843-divination-and-awakening?p=1040852#post1040852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I am referring to the Time Spell Divination, which seems pretty powerful and open. I assumed the answer was yes, but it seemed kind of interesting since in 1E that was assumed impossible.<br /> <br /> Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case you absolutely can. In 2e all the examples of using the spell involve targeting a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:44:48-08:00","id":1040868,"title":"","content":"Hey PenDragon,<br /> <br /> Thanks for the quick response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:13:48-08:00","id":1040887,"title":"","content":"I can't say for sure but I think the answer might be yes, I recall a blink and you miss it reference to interfering with Awakening being one of the topics that will be covered in SoS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:36:45-08:00","id":1040903,"title":"","content":"Alright, along the same line I suppose of reasoning.<br /> <br /> Strings of Fate<br /> <br /> Can you make it so someone Awakens?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:39:19-08:00","id":1040905,"title":"","content":"I always ruled that Awakenings happen in spite of Fate, Destiny and Time. I like the metaphysical implications (that Awakening is such a great act of magic that it can deny and overrule &quot;certain&quot; Fate and &quot;certain&quot; Future) and I like how it impacts the setting - this way each person might turn from a Sleeper into Awakened in blink of an eye, and it makes spotting new Awakened harder, which in turn is more dramatic; I prefer when Mages find Orders themselves, or are found out only after they had some time on their hands with magic, giving them room to grow bad habits or do Stuff That's A Very Good Idea From Your Perspective But Actually Terrible Idea If You Have Bigger Picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:44:53-08:00","id":1040909,"title":"","content":"Hey WHW,<br /> <br /> I agree with you, I like the pretty much unpredictability of such things. Its just according to RAW it seems to be pretty obvious that you can in fact determine if someone is going to Awaken, maybe not the exact second but it does appear a simple Divination can yield a result of &quot;Dennis will Awaken sometime in the upcoming year.&quot; or perhaps &quot;Dennis will Awaken when something catches his attention that he refuses to let go.&quot;<br /> <br /> In a sense, based on my understanding from the RAW it seems that it becomes a recruitment battle for members, which seemed to happen in 1E due to unexplained circumstances. So, it does appear there was/is someway to actually get a good read that someone is going to awaken, maybe not exactly but that they will awaken and should thus be monitored for recruitment. Of course, this kind of makes things interesting when you place this into the equation of a Cold War between the Seers and the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:45:39-08:00","id":1040910,"title":"","content":"Signs of Sorcery will give more information on awakenings in general, but I'm pretty sure that one of the things covered in it will be how to spot someone that is awakening. As to pushing it along, I'm pretty sure that's a hard no. Only Archmasters are capable of that, and even then it's considered a thing you don't do since it's extremely likely it will cause the person to be a banisher.<br /> <br /> Er, I guess I meant causing, rather than pushing. They're different, and the latter IS supposed to be covered in SoS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:48:27-08:00","id":1040914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040843-divination-and-awakening?p=1040905#post1040905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always ruled that Awakenings happen in spite of Fate, Destiny and Time. I like the metaphysical implications (that Awakening is such a great act of magic that it can deny and overrule &quot;certain&quot; Fate and &quot;certain&quot; Future) and I like how it impacts the setting - this way each person might turn from a Sleeper into Awakened in blink of an eye, and it makes spotting new Awakened harder, which in turn is more dramatic; I prefer when Mages find Orders themselves, or are found out only after they had some time on their hands with magic, giving them room to grow bad habits or do Stuff That's A Very Good Idea From Your Perspective But Actually Terrible Idea If You Have Bigger Picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a Banisher factory to me. <br /> <br /> The Awakened have rules. If there is no one there to hold your hand when you Awaken, you're going to transgress against these rules. When you buy mice to feed your pet python, you're not going to realize sacrificing rodents to draw mana is going to make you roll your wisdom. <br /> <br /> If Fate and Time can't track Awakenings, there is no way for either the Diamond or the Seers to spot newly Awakened mages, which would mean they would have no way of establishing a society of the Awakened. Awakening is hard, it's not like losing your virginity or defending your doctoral thesis. You're entering a new normative system, and if there's no-one there to guide you you're going to do things that fall outside of its rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:49:22-08:00","id":1040915,"title":"","content":"Hey Falcon777,<br /> <br /> I think that was also included in a comment by Dave Brookshaw in the GMC Stop-gap Rules about creating a Major Template without Archmastery, but that may have been written before Strings of Fate was considered. I mean the RAW seems to allow such a thing, but I would rule that most likely by tampering with such a Fate you would 99.9999999% of the time cause a Banisher to be created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:01:45-08:00","id":1040924,"title":"","content":"So, just because Divination could confirm if someone will Awaken the future isn't set so they might not, vice versa you could get a negative result and then later it turns out they do Awaken. There's also the limitations of scale, Mages can't check the future of everyone in the world. On the other hand, Prophecy can give you the steps you need to take to stumble across someone who is newly Awakened and you only have to use yourself as a Subject of the spell. The downside is that you're then locking in your own personal future good or bad. Though you're allowed to deviate, but might miss the chance to meet the newbie Mage, or might suffer outside interference from some other Mage's Time magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:13:54-08:00","id":1040931,"title":"","content":"Why does it matter what the RAW say if it contradicts the setting? Any RPG has gaps and contradictions, as long as the game isn't totally stalled, just make a judgement and move on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:30:11-08:00","id":1040942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>logos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040843-divination-and-awakening?p=1040914#post1040914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sounds like a Banisher factory to me.<br /> <br /> The Awakened have rules. If there is no one there to hold your hand when you Awaken, you're going to transgress against these rules. When you buy mice to feed your pet python, you're not going to realize sacrificing rodents to draw mana is going to make you roll your wisdom.<br /> <br /> If Fate and Time can't track Awakenings, there is no way for either the Diamond or the Seers to spot newly Awakened mages, which would mean they would have no way of establishing a society of the Awakened. Awakening is hard, it's not like losing your virginity or defending your doctoral thesis. You're entering a new normative system, and if there's no-one there to guide you you're going to do things that fall outside of its rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is exactly what I want! Maybe minus the Banisher factory part, as &quot;poorly educated&quot; doesn't automatically mean you are a Wisdom-less poor soul. When all people are following the rules and never doing non-non stuff, there isn't much story potential outside of political bickering, and I find that not very attractive. Flawed individuals produce most perfect stories.<br /> I think that asking yourself &quot;what do I want in my setting?&quot; is extremely important, so exploring both options and checking them for obvious and unobvious consequences is super important when prepping a Mage game. So I'm going to show how I handle it, why I think it's cool, and maybe why someone might not find it ideal for their game.<br /> <br /> Alternative to Fate/Time tracking isn't actually that hard, and I find it much more exciting from GMing and player standpoint, as it breeds more conflict and uncertainity. Newly Awakened are going to be drawn towards Obsessions, and there are certain activities that they might find themselves doing. So as a Awakening-Spotter, you look for these patterns. You study what are 101 Typical Signs That Someone Awakened In This Neighborhood. You look for massive rodent purchases, you look up weird power spikes, you arrange &quot;baby's first&quot; Mysteries as a catch for naive Awakened hoping that one of them will start digging into it, coming to you. You rush to massive Paradox releases. You investigate, observe and hope that you will find them first, before...before they hurt themselves, hurt someone else, or get grabbed by someone else. In many aspects, this becomes like a Spy Game, with careful investigations and a lot of pretending to look cool and competent and knowing exactly what you are doing, while in reality you are just tracing shadows and stumbling in the darkness with a tiny candle. Which is, for me, an essence of Mage Mystery Experience. <br /> Of course, this places a lot of weight upon recruiters shoulders; they might catch up to a recruit after days, weeks or even months after their Awakening. Some, they miss altogether. It makes Awakened Societies smaller and less stable, without constant supply of students and newcomers. I personally prefer Consilia to be small, and with a ratio of something like 20 non-mage &quot;auxiliary&quot; members per full and true Mage member, so it doesn't bother me that much. Again, I'm not very fond of political struggles and prefer to focus on smaller, more local and less centralized societies, with investigation and Mysteries being the main meat of the game. And &quot;Spot The Awakened&quot; is a fantastic, thrilling, real stakes involving Mystery, especially for Guardians of the Veil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:34:32-08:00","id":1040943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040843-divination-and-awakening?p=1040931#post1040931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does it matter what the RAW say if it contradicts the setting? Any RPG has gaps and contradictions, as long as the game isn't totally stalled, just make a judgement and move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it does contradict the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:23:10-08:00","id":1041024,"title":"","content":"I suspect the Seers have this one relatively easy - the Tyrants can just notify their servants in dreams, omens, background noise or whatever, if the newly Awakened mage is important to their rule.<br /> <br /> Too bad &quot;important&quot; can sometimes mean &quot;he will turn against you and join the Pentacle, leaving you ousted from your seat so that a more capable servant rises to fill it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T23:11:40-08:00","id":1041119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040843-divination-and-awakening?p=1040903#post1040903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, along the same line I suppose of reasoning.<br /> <br /> Strings of Fate<br /> <br /> Can you make it so someone Awakens?<br /> <br /> Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost every attempt to force an Awakening fails, or creates a Banisher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T23:35:33-08:00","id":1041130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040843-divination-and-awakening?p=1040943#post1040943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it does contradict the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a major element that would radically alter how a number of different organisations work and it's never been mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T00:46:41-08:00","id":1041142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040843-divination-and-awakening?p=1041130#post1041130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a major element that would radically alter how a number of different organisations work and it's never been mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really? As I pointed out, it's probably going to be in SoS, and tracking Awakening via magic isn't a great idea because a) The future isn't set, and b) has an element of risk that's best avoided by using mundane systems like the Labyrinth to detect new and potential Mages. It's a far cry from manufacturing Awakening or getting predictable results from tracking potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T01:25:22-08:00","id":1041147,"title":"","content":"Getting technical about it, you can use strings of fate to put someone into a high-stress situation where they come up against the Lie. <br /> <br /> But *Awakening* is, mechanically, an act of Imperial magic cast by the relevant Watchtower, according to their own unknown criteria and conditions. You can't predict their actions, you can't make them choose someone.<br /> <br /> All the Awakened can do is increasingly-elaborate versions of causing car crashes to see if someone survives as a Moros. Archnasters can, in theory, reproduce what the watchtowers do in granting a Path, but the results almost always end up as Banishers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T01:37:18-08:00","id":1041150,"title":"","content":"I love the plot potential for awakening gambits like these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T02:59:59-08:00","id":1041165,"title":"","content":"*However*, once an Awakening experience gets underway, it's like banging a gong in the Supernal World of the corresponding Path, and although it's probably not a good idea many mages try to insert themselves as characters in an in-progress Mystery Play. You have to have the right Path and a loose enough grasp of morals to invade someone elses' one direct contact with Truth. The results can be enlightening, or tragic, or tragically enlightening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T03:12:26-08:00","id":1041167,"title":"","content":"Setting up the car crashes is the whole schtick of the Awakening Gambit legacy if I remember correctly. I'm curious though, since nearly every attempt to force an awakening ends up creating a Banisher, I wonder if there is a force working to create Banishers since you'd think some Archmaster level Mages would have it work out sometimes even if they were experimenting randomly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T03:17:13-08:00","id":1041169,"title":"","content":"The book also states that a person without the urge of questioning things and go after knowledge never awakens. She may see things, know things, be aware of things, but tries the blue pill (as a Matrix metaphore).<br /> <br /> So a person can get to a state of soul evolution where she can awake, being chosen by a watchtower or some other metaphisical explanation (I thought being chosen by a watchtower was only 1st edition, and that in 2nd it was an optional explanation). But this doesn't mean she will awaken.<br /> <br /> Mages could know the state of evolution of a human soul to awaken, know what synchronicities raise the chances of a person to awaken, analyce her personality, if this person has the will to pursue knowledge and pierce lies, but still don't know for sure if she will awake or not until she awakes.<br /> <br /> It is like predicting weather. All reports say it will be a sunny day, all weather news say it will be a good day to go picnic, but in ten minutes the sky suddenly gets cloudy and starts to rain. And then all TV news speak about this rain, and don't understand why it has rained, why it hasn't been a sunny day when all the factors for a sunny day where there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T11:29:42-08:00","id":1041361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040843-divination-and-awakening?p=1041147#post1041147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But *Awakening* is, mechanically, an act of Imperial magic cast by the relevant Watchtower, according to their own unknown criteria and conditions. You can't predict their actions, you can't make them choose someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imperial spells require Quintessences, though, and Quintessences often involve the actions of Traveler-scale beings, yes? Trying to force an Awakening is a bad idea, but trying to fulfill the Quintessence necessary for a Watchtower to Awaken someone, thereby giving as many people the opportunity to Awaken as possible is something I can see.<br /> <br /> Of course, certain Quintessences could be incredibly immoral, like repeatedly causing car crashes just in case one of them was the Quintessence necessary to get a new Moros, as you bring up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:29:40-08:00","id":1041403,"title":"","content":"This reminds me of the movie &quot;Unbreakable&quot;, where Samuel L. Jackson's character was causing disasters and waiting to see if someone survived.<br /> \u200bPersonally I think Fate &amp; Time could be used to identify if a specific individual will Awaken and even when, I also think that future wouldn't be fixed and the seeker's knowledge of it alone maybe enough to prevent it, either through his interference or his absence in trying to avoid interfering, and let's not forget that he may not be the only Mage involved.<br /> \u200bIn the end if what you want is a setting where no one can accurately predict Awakenings, just rule that the Watchtowers themselves are shielded from Fate &amp; Time and that as a consequence no one can tell what they are going to do. This person has all of the hallmarks of an Awakening but who knows if the Watchtowers will reach out to him.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:45:29-08:00","id":1041489,"title":"","content":"Now I'm curious about what this means about the Guardians' Labyrinth, and whether it basically boils down to &quot;The Guardians have figured out a reliable Quintessence to turn people into candidates for the Watchtowers to Awaken (should they choose to&quot;. Possibly thanks to the work of some Ascended Guardian Exemplar at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:53:18-08:00","id":1041536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040843-divination-and-awakening?p=1041489#post1041489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm curious about what this means about the Guardians' Labyrinth, and whether it basically boils down to &quot;The Guardians have figured out a reliable Quintessence to turn people into candidates for the Watchtowers to Awaken (should they choose to&quot;. Possibly thanks to the work of some Ascended Guardian Exemplar at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Guardians don't use the Labyrinth to encourage Awakenings, they use it for the opposite. Only the worthy are able to see through their Lie to Awaken, but it's not a proving ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T18:02:13-08:00","id":1041599,"title":"","content":"That's... the opposite of my understanding of the Labyrinth. Yes it's used to dissuade the unworthy, but it's also the only proven method the Diamond has to trigger Awakenings in the worthy.<br /> <br /> It does both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T18:24:31-08:00","id":1041613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040843-divination-and-awakening?p=1041599#post1041599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... the opposite of my understanding of the Labyrinth. Yes it's used to dissuade the unworthy, but it's also the only proven method the Diamond has to trigger Awakenings in the worthy.<br /> <br /> It does both.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, it's not proven method for triggering Awakenings it's a method for keeping an eye on potential Awakenings or other mortal trouble makers. Second, it's designed to be a curiosity satiating experience leading the occupants down never ending and pointless rabbit trails away from Awakening because Guardians are hardcore meritocratic. Third, the SL are the ones that create &quot;Awakening&quot; cults. They actually employ a methodology that attempts to cultivate Sleepers to be more accepting of magic before eventually giving them full blown magical revelations intended to shock them out of Sleep. Their methods are no more reliable.<br /> <br /> The Guardians are usually the first to know about a new Mage because of the Labyrinth, but the existence of such a Mage is an accidental byproduct of the Labyrinth not working equally well on everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-31-2017, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}